# Old domain → new domain. The site was executivewellnesshousing.com until September 16, 2026.
# These only match while the old domain is still attached to this Netlify site as a domain alias
# — remove the alias and old links stop redirecting. 301 tells Google to move its rankings over;
# the "!" makes the rule win even though the requested file exists.
https://executivewellnesshousing.com/*      https://executivewellnesssuites.com/:splat  301!
https://www.executivewellnesshousing.com/*  https://executivewellnesssuites.com/:splat  301!
http://executivewellnesshousing.com/*       https://executivewellnesssuites.com/:splat  301!
http://www.executivewellnesshousing.com/*   https://executivewellnesssuites.com/:splat  301!

# housing.executivewellnesssuites.com — the lodging landing page, a plain HTML file at
# client/public/housing/index.html. These only match while the subdomain is attached to this
# Netlify site as a domain alias.
#
# A domain alias serves the WHOLE site, so the third rule sends every other path on the
# subdomain to the main domain; without it, every page would exist twice. The last two keep the
# page from also living at executivewellnesssuites.com/housing. Deploy previews have their own
# hostname, so none of these match there and the page previews at /housing/.
http://housing.executivewellnesssuites.com/*   https://housing.executivewellnesssuites.com/:splat  301!
https://housing.executivewellnesssuites.com/   /housing/index.html                                200!
https://housing.executivewellnesssuites.com/*  https://executivewellnesssuites.com/:splat         301!
https://executivewellnesssuites.com/housing    https://housing.executivewellnesssuites.com/       301!
https://executivewellnesssuites.com/housing/*  https://housing.executivewellnesssuites.com/       301!

# Netlify serves existing static files first; this is the last-resort SPA fallback
# so deep links and refreshes never 404.
/*    /index.html   200
